From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:17:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Find the databases of earlier sessions in the
 client storage registry

The IndexedDB manager only knew the databases it had opened since it
started (`self.databases`). After a restart, databases() missed every
database of an earlier session, and deleteDatabase of one reported an
old version of 0 and left the database, files and registry entry, in
place, so its next open found the old data. Upstream has the same code.
Open already found such a database, since the registry's create looks an
existing one up.

Open and delete now look a database that the manager hasn't opened up in
the client storage registry, at step 4, once the request is at the front
of its connection queue (new OpenRequestState::Locating): an open with
the registry's create (lookup or create, step 6), a delete with
FindDatabase. This runs on the manager's client storage thread, like the
storage proxy map, and comes back as
IndexedDBThreadMsg::DatabaseLocated; only the front request of a queue
gets there, and only it changes the database's registry entry, so the
answer can't be stale. An open then opens the engine on the manager
thread as before. A delete of a database found there has no connection
to wait for: it reads the version the database committed last
(SqlEngine::committed_version, without opening an engine, so a database
of another schema version, which an open would reset, counts as 0),
deletes the database and its registry entry, and reports the version. A
database whose version can't be read, such as a corrupt one, is deleted
all the same with version 0, as Gecko does.

databases() sends a StorageBottleSource (GetDatabases has a third
field). The manager lists the bottle's databases in the registry on that
thread (IndexedDBThreadMsg::DatabasesListed), then reports the databases
it has open with the version of their last committed upgrade, as before,
and every other listed one with its committed version from its file;
version 0 is left out.

The manager now closes its databases before it acknowledges Exit, as the
message's documentation says, so that a restarted manager doesn't meet
the old connections.

A stored database of version 0, which a session that ended during the
database's first upgrade leaves behind, opens as a new one, as
databases() already treats it: an open without a version upgrades it
from 0 to 1. It returned a connection at version 0 without stores, so a
page that creates its stores in upgradeneeded failed with that database
for good (P5 review S1). Reading a stored database's version first
checks that its file exists (SqlExecutor::exists), so databases() and a
delete create no empty database file in a registry directory that has
none (N2). A registry lookup or list that can't be handed to the client
storage calls thread fails its request or databases() call (N4).

Validation: host `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits`: 155 passed, 1 skipped (new: tests/indexeddb.rs test_indexeddb_databases_of_an_earlier_session_are_listed_deleted_and_opened and test_indexeddb_database_of_an_earlier_session_is_deleted_without_being_listed, which restart the storage threads on the same data, and backend committed_version_of_a_stored_database, each on every backend compiled in); DAYU200 unit tests: the two restart tests and committed_version_of_a_stored_database pass with RDB only (RDB registry and engine) and with both backends (both registry engines); host SM and QuickJS IndexedDB/ 4,484 of 4,511 and /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 312 of 312 SM, 310 of 312 QuickJS (interface lists, as before), every result as expected (unchanged: WPT runs in one session); 10 back-to-back host runs per engine: SM every result as expected in 10 of 10, QuickJS in 9 of 10 (one transaction-inflight-worker-terminate subtest, also 2 of 10 with P5.2's binary); DAYU200 (QuickJS + RDB) IndexedDB/ 4,468 to 4,476 of 4,511 in 5 runs over 2 boots (P5.2: 4,464), unexpected only idb-partitioned-coverage and file_support, as before; after the P5 review fixes: 158 passed, 1 skipped at this commit, with the new restart test test_indexeddb_database_left_at_version_0_by_an_earlier_session_opens_as_new (it gets a connection at version 0 without the fix) and committed_version_of_a_stored_database checking that an empty directory stays empty; the P5 review's crash probe (kill -9 during a first upgrade, then a versionless open) gives upgradeneeded from 0 to 1 in 2 of 2 runs on the stack tip, where it gave a connection at version 0
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent designed the registry lookups for open, delete and databases, implemented them and the restart tests, and measured the result; the P5 review fixes for version 0 databases, version probes and lookups that can't be handed over, with the restart test)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
